{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-81ce131a2b76ef4a", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Transition Matching Distillation for Fast Video Generation\narXiv: 2601.09881\nAuthors: Weili Nie, Julius Berner, Nanye Ma, Chao Liu, Saining Xie, Arash Vahdat\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A novel distillation framework for video diffusion that distills long denoising trajectories into a compact few-step probability transition process.\n  2. A decoupled diffusion backbone design that decomposes the teacher model into a semantic backbone and a recurrent flow head for hierarchical distillation with flexible inner flow refinement.\n  3. A two-stage training strategy consisting of transition matching adaption to convert the flow head into a conditional flow map followed by distribution matching distillation with flow head rollout.\n  4. Comprehensive empirical validation demonstrating state-of-the-art trade-offs between speed and quality in few-step video generation when distilling Wan2.1 1.3B and 14B models.\n===\n# History-Guided Video Diffusion\narXiv: 2502.06764\nAuthors: Kiwhan Song, Boyuan Chen, Max Simchowitz, Yilun Du, Russ Tedrake, Vincent Sitzmann\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose the Diffusion Forcing Transformer, a video diffusion framework that enables flexible conditioning on any portion of the input history.\n  2. We introduce History Guidance, a family of history-conditioned guidance methods that significantly enhance sample consistency, motion dynamics, and visual quality.\n  3. We empirically demonstrate state-of-the-art performance and new capabilities in long video generation, supported by a theoretical justification of the training objective.", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "e960e52e-184e-4e79-9d32-fc28a8353a5b", "uuid": "847c8697-cc50-4ba4-8b26-178eb0b4c6bd", "timestamp": "2026-08-07T09:48:37.492Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Transition Matching Distillation for Fast Video Generation\narXiv: 2601.09881\nAuthors: Weili Nie, Julius Berner, Nanye Ma, Chao Liu, Saining Xie, Arash Vahdat\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A novel distillation framework for video diffusion that distills long denoising trajectories into a compact few-step probability transition process.\n  2. A decoupled diffusion backbone design that decomposes the teacher model into a semantic backbone and a recurrent flow head for hierarchical distillation with flexible inner flow refinement.\n  3. A two-stage training strategy consisting of transition matching adaption to convert the flow head into a conditional flow map followed by distribution matching distillation with flow head rollout.\n  4. Comprehensive empirical validation demonstrating state-of-the-art trade-offs between speed and quality in few-step video generation when distilling Wan2.1 1.3B and 14B models.\n===\n# History-Guided Video Diffusion\narXiv: 2502.06764\nAuthors: Kiwhan Song, Boyuan Chen, Max Simchowitz, Yilun Du, Russ Tedrake, Vincent Sitzmann\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose the Diffusion Forcing Transformer, a video diffusion framework that enables flexible conditioning on any portion of the input history.\n  2. We introduce History Guidance, a family of history-conditioned guidance methods that significantly enhance sample consistency, motion dynamics, and visual quality.\n  3. We empirically demonstrate state-of-the-art performance and new capabilities in long video generation, supported by a theoretical justification of the training objective.", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
